            <ArticleTitle>Pitfalls in the diagnosis of juvenile rheumatoid arthritis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1015-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There are many conditions that produce chronic arthritis in childhood, including JRA. The pitfalls associated with proper diagnosis involve underrecognition, misrecognition, and overrecognition of symptoms and signs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
